<title>USA: Invivo Corp Q1 net, share lower.</title>
<headline>Invivo Corp Q1 net, share lower.</headline>
<dateline>FREMONT, Calif. 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>($ 000 omitted, except for per-share and share data)</p>
<p>					   Three Months Ended</p>
<p>						   Sept. 30,</p>
<p>					     1996	 1995</p>
<p> Net sales				 7,892	7,842</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold		    3,931	3,892</p>
<p>   Gross profit			  3,961	3,950</p>
<p>Total operating</p>
<p>	 expenses			  3,927	2,652</p>
<p> Income from operations		   34	1,298</p>
<p> Net income				    3	  820</p>
<p>Net income per</p>
<p>   common share			    .00	  .24</p>
<p>Average number of common</p>
<p>   shares outstanding	    3,417,664  3,460,332</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610  </p>
<p>NOTE: The company said first quarter 1996 results reflect the planned 50 percent increase in selling, general and administrative expenses to support the launch of Invivo Research subsidiary's new Millennia portable multi-parameter vital signs monitor.</p>
